{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216416-patrician-houses","id":1216416,"title":"Patrician Houses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-07T18:48:05-07:00","id":1216416,"title":"Patrician Houses","content":"I find it kind of interesting that none of these have ever been named or described. Maybe that will change in the Realm book, but I thought up a few in the mean time. These are very short conceptual summaries, mostly for background details for adopted Dynasts and minor players in the Realm.<br /> <br /> House Jada - Rumored to be touched by blood of the Mountain Folk, which makes Dynasts wary about adopting their Exalted. One of the largest non-jade mining powers in the Realm, well respected for their foundry work in iron, bronze, and steel. The Earth Aspected House matriarch is the original founder, a Lost Egg who distinguished herself in the Legions before settling down investing her earnings in mining and smithing concerns. (Earth)<br /> <br /> Houses Caveth and Gemar - rival olive farming powers claiming descent from the same Wood Aspected male ancestor via two different mortal wives. Caveth's reputation is as simple earthy joyseekers, with some unsavery reputations of illegal god-worship. Gemar is seen as more spiritually focused and ruthlessly passionate, trying to fan the flames of their essence toward producing Exalted - with some accusations of heretical worship of the Dragons themselves (particularly Hesiesh and Sextes Jylis). The two Houses have a Montegue/Capulet, Hatfield/McCoy, Blackwood/Bracken irrational longstanding vendetta (Wood)<br /> <br /> House Opor - founded by a mortal family that elevated themselves through pure financial success building a fishing fleet, they have since taken in no insignificant amount of dragon-blood via marriage to Found-Eggs after their Legion service; particularly Water Aspects. Every stereotype of salty fisherfolk and upjumped bourgeoise at the same time (Water)<br /> <br /> House Demes - a merchant house highly invested in caravans, cultivating a reputation as reliable middle-men between other Houses and the territories of the Realm. Some have even suggested they have ambitions to be the Realm's full fledged response to the Guild. In truth, they're one of the remaining lineages descended from House Iselsi, and when it's Dragon-Blooded are adopted into Great Houses, the Vendetta places its agents throughout the Dynasty. (Water)<br /> <br /> House Rumel - Under the Empress, this House distinguished itself through the service its mortal members in the Legions, while the retirees built financial power through using their Legion connections for diversified investment. Since the reorganization of the Legions under the Great Houses though, they have much less ability to distinguish themselves without fully aligning themselves under one of the Great House's thrall (Earth)<br /> <br /> House Avev - One of the older remaining houses founded by a Lost Egg after their Legion service, this House's wealth has been built on silk farming and fashion, with its designers and silk merchants being sought in the hall of Dynastic power and courtly intrigue (Fire)<br /> <br /> House Haoka - One of the few remaining Shogunate Gens, these hyper-traditionalists have built their wealth on rice farming and rice-wine (Fire)<br /> <br /> House Keben - this house has made itself invaluable to the Thousand Scales by turning their forested land holdings toward the sole purpose of paper manufacturing. They are at the forefront of printing in general (opening the possibility of a Lunar strike before they can actually make non-artifact movable type printing press a reality) (Air)<br /> <br /> House Ashara - Once wealthy orchardists claiming a lineage back to the Gens of the Shogunate, and governing the city of their namesake, they now cling to dust as the Tarpan Wastes expand to take everything they once had (Air)<br /> <br /> House Betot - Major ranching power, and increasingly some of the most outspoken abolitionists in the Realm (Wood)<br /> <br /> House Yiju - Founded by a mortal sorcerer, and even without access to the Heptagram, its mortal scions are encouraged to seek out sorcerous intiation and study thaumaturgical arts. They're rumored to have been tained by demon blood over the years. Their services are highly valuable to Patricians looking for Sorcerous services outside the auspices of the Heptagram trained Sorcerers of the Great Houses; but they're highly stigmatized and seen as unclean making it next to impossible for them to try and marry-in Dragon blood (-)<br /> <br /> House Bal - Descends from a mortal son of the Empress (Berit's brother actually) and lower born Dragon-Blooded wife. Denied Great House status themselves and never incorporated into one of the rising Houses like Nellens in its day or V'neef more recently, the Empress has most notably charged Dragon-Blooded born of the line with the unofficially hereditary heading of the Treasury. The only member of the family to ever abuse the post was caught by his own son, and executed, so the Empress preserved the family's hold on it and no one has ever made the mistake again, so there's little direct profit from one member holding the position. The prestige is helpful however, and mortal Bals serve throughout the Imperial Service, while those Dragon-Blooded not directly in line for heading the Treasury are swiftly adopted by Great Houses. Marrying a mortal of House Bal is seen as essentially the next best thing to marrying into a Great House for Found-Eggs after the Legion service - they see themselves as first among Patricians. (Water)<br /> <br /> House Amon - A Shogunate-era Gen that would likely be utterly forgotten were it not for its Exalted scion Amon Mora serving as Keeper of the First Imperial Seal. A few mortal lines distantly related to Mora maintain the family name as well - some of whom bitterly suspect his influence actively prevented them from being uplifted into House V'neef (as he didn't want the familial connection to be seen as biasing him toward a House). One wing of the family controls an inland river port and surrounding grazing land. Another slightly more successful wing is invested in vineyards. All in all though, their near total lack of new Exaltations has kept them near the bottom of the Patrician social barrel without a leg up into the Imperial Service (Mora never doing more than helping provide contact with a strict mentor who MIGHT get a job for a worthy pupil, but it would have to be entirely earned). (-)<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Your own ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-09-2018, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T19:46:00-07:00","id":1216440,"title":"","content":"Overall very good! Thanks for the read!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T21:29:16-07:00","id":1216481,"title":"","content":"Is this meant to be all of them? Or just a sampling?<br /> <br /> I always figured the Patrician class, being mortals and whose houses dont have much official clout, would have several family lines, unlike the Dynasty (which is deliberatly limited to a few houses to keep powrr concentrated)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T04:30:29-07:00","id":1216563,"title":"","content":"Canonically we've have had a few it's just that Compass: Blessed Isle insisted on calling them clans, presumably to avoid confusing them with the Great Houses but as this thread demonstrates it didn't combat their erasure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T04:35:18-07:00","id":1216565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216416-patrician-houses?p=1216563#post1216563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canonically we've have had a few it's just that Compass: Blessed Isle insisted on calling them clans, presumably to avoid confusing them with the Great Houses but as this thread demonstrates it didn't combat their erasure.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI can't recall, did the book actually list them somewhere, or were they distributed around among subjects related to any of their purviews?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T04:42:33-07:00","id":1216570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216416-patrician-houses?p=1216565#post1216565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't recall, did the book actually list them somewhere, or were they distributed around among subjects related to any of their purviews?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter. They often turn up when talking about Prefects and other mortal government figures and sometimes breeding the Dynast\u2019s specialised pets such as the Portee Ivory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T04:51:44-07:00","id":1216575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216416-patrician-houses?p=1216570#post1216570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They often turn up when talking about Prefects and other mortal government figures and sometimes breeding the Dynast\u2019s specialised pets such as the Portee Ivory.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's what I thought. I definitely remembered the animal breeders. I could hardly fault somebody for forgetting them, being conveyed like that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T06:07:25-07:00","id":1216595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216416-patrician-houses?p=1216575#post1216575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThat's what I thought. I definitely remembered the animal breeders. I could hardly fault somebody for forgetting them, being conveyed like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh the execution was a shitshow, but I think the animal breeders were on the verge of a clever use of patricians families because it gave them a memorable hook and connection to the Great Houses.<br /> <br /> For example: Years ago my group took note of the fact that The Portee Ivory and Blackstar Mastiff were both bred in Lord's Crossing Dominion and therefore House Tepet has access to some very successful dog breeders. Suddenly a PCs mother was dealing with her grief by turning all her attention to her hunting dogs.<br /> If most Great Houses had something like that (obviously not all animals because that would be cliche as fuck) it would be much easier to bring them into Dragon-Blooded games.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T11:13:30-07:00","id":1216746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216416-patrician-houses?p=1216481#post1216481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this meant to be all of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god no. It's just a few ideas. I assume there are at least hundreds of Patrician Houses on the Blessed Isle!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-08-2018, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T22:51:21-07:00","id":1216906,"title":"","content":"Added Houses Bal and Amon - both with prominent Exalted members in the Empress' direct service, but whose rank and file mortal members are at opposing ends of the Patrician-prestige spectrum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-09-2018, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T02:18:57-07:00","id":1217607,"title":"","content":"My own 2e character was a son of House Wu, who were officially into trade and tea sales but were also secretly trying to make a smuggling pact with <b><i>The Mask of Winters</i></b> to undermine the guild and usurp a position into Great House status. Wu Sheng-Tong Exalted upon fleeing from the sight of the Mask and then being savagely beaten by his Terrestrial elder brother, slaying him in an instant and going on the run. He had an ... interesting relationship with the Mask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T08:11:00-07:00","id":1403232,"title":"","content":"Must admit i have played more, at least directly, with cadet houses and unexalted branches of the Dinasty trying to get a leg up again than patrician houses.<br /> <br /> That said my longest playing DB, Sinasi Keldor, had a propensity for social networking on all steps of the social ladder during his, quite extensive, travels that would make a Nellens proud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-17-2020, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T16:43:02-07:00","id":1403435,"title":"","content":"Ok, in line with a character I've been sorta working on....<br /> <br /> howlikely would Patrician houses be to support a movement to depose the Dynastic Houses? Especially if the leader was one of the Empress's younger children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T17:14:49-07:00","id":1403441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216416-patrician-houses?p=1403435#post1403435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, in line with a character I've been sorta working on....<br /> <br /> howlikely would Patrician houses be to support a movement to depose the Dynastic Houses? Especially if the leader was one of the Empress's younger children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, i think one of the plotlines in the chapter intros of DB: WFHW involves exactly such a thing - except for the child of Empress bit that is, though that might be a way to add extra legitimacy to the movement while opposing the Great Houses' leaders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T20:20:25-07:00","id":1403477,"title":"","content":"Oh, and she has outside support from the Silver Pact since she is secretly Lunar Exalted<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T10:33:57-07:00","id":1403686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216416-patrician-houses?p=1403435#post1403435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, in line with a character I've been sorta working on....<br /> <br /> howlikely would Patrician houses be to support a movement to depose the Dynastic Houses? Especially if the leader was one of the Empress's younger children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not very. Remember, that they will be mostly thinking about improving the situation of their own House, and won't be gambling its very existence for some not well defined gains unless the payoff they can envision is really massive, they're very desperate, or both.You may potentially see them willing to sign on the idea of deposing a specific Dynastic House (especially if it's not a house they're in a good relation with/dependant on), or joining a plot that might end up with elevating their own house to the Dynastic heights. Willing to face massive risks in order to bring down the whole system, to create a chaos in which some patrician houses might get a lot of power, but most would likely just end up destroyed? They have way too much to lose. There might be a few particians willing to join such a cause, and some more might support it less directly, but the majority would probably rather prefer to either not get involved,or even to actively try to stop such an idea before someone (meaning - them) gets hurt.<br /> <br /> Now, the idea of pushing for changes where some rights and influences of Patricians within the Realm get increased a bit, at the cost of some of the privileges of the Dynasts might be something much more appealing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","user":"Astralporing","date":". 07-20-2020, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T10:45:35-07:00","id":1403687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216416-patrician-houses?p=1403686#post1403686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not very. Remember, that they will be mostly thinking about improving the situation of their own House, and won't be gambling its very existence for some not well defined gains unless the payoff they can envision is really massive, they're very desperate, or both.You may potentially see them willing to sign on the idea of deposing a specific Dynastic House (especially if it's not a house they're in a good relation with/dependant on), or joining a plot that might end up with elevating their own house to the Dynastic heights. Willing to face massive risks in order to bring down the whole system, to create a chaos in which some patrician houses might get a lot of power, but most would likely just end up destroyed? They have way too much to lose. There might be a few particians willing to join such a cause, and some more might support it less directly, but the majority would probably rather prefer to either not get involved,or even to actively try to stop such an idea before someone (meaning - them) gets hurt.<br /> <br /> Now, the idea of pushing for changes where some rights and influences of Patricians within the Realm get increased a bit, at the cost of some of the privileges of the Dynasts might be something much more appealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you gotten to read What Fire Has Wrought yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T15:32:51-07:00","id":1406159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216416-patrician-houses?p=1403687#post1403687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you gotten to read What Fire Has Wrought yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I don't remember anything there that would contradict my views above though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T15:34:58-07:00","id":1406160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216416-patrician-houses?p=1406159#post1406159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. I don't remember anything there that would contradict my views above though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The chapter fiction concerning Kingfisher Swift strikes close. <i>The Realm</i> expands upon it as an interest of the patrician clans of the Scarlet Prefecture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T15:50:36-07:00","id":1406162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216416-patrician-houses?p=1403686#post1403686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the idea of pushing for changes where some rights and influences of Patricians within the Realm get increased a bit, at the cost of some of the privileges of the Dynasts might be something much more appealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that kinda thing is that the ruling class of the Realm are literally superhuman demigods who are venerated by the state religion as enlightened bodhisattvas borderline above the concept of law itself. Any patrician advocating for this is committing <i>literal</i> heresy in a way that isn't really mirrored by any real-life precedent because we don't have a class of objectively superhuman demigods in any human society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T16:33:58-07:00","id":1406173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216416-patrician-houses?p=1406162#post1406162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">above the concept of law itself</div> </div> </div> </div>This is absolutely not the case. The Realm could not exist, let alone function, if it had no laws to restrict the impulses, excesses, and ambitions of the Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T16:34:15-07:00","id":1406175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216416-patrician-houses?p=1403477#post1403477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and she has outside support from the Silver Pact since she is secretly Lunar Exalted</div> </div> </div> </div>So your character is a Patrician who Exalted as a Lunar?<br /> <br /> If she\u2019s a Lunar and a member of the Silver Pact she would probably support a movement to overthrow the current regime if the movement\u2019s leader promised to stop using the Wyld Hunt to hunt down Lunars and allow them a voice in the Deliberative. If the movement is led by one of the Empress\u2019s children it\u2019s very unlikely she (the leader of the movement) would allow the Dynastic Houses to be completely ousted from power since she would be a member of the Dynasty herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T18:22:16-07:00","id":1406200,"title":"","content":"No, not a Patrician","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T20:24:01-07:00","id":1406208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216416-patrician-houses?p=1403435#post1403435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, in line with a character I've been sorta working on....<br /> <br /> howlikely would Patrician houses be to support a movement to depose the Dynastic Houses? Especially if the leader was one of the Empress's younger children.</div> </div> </div> </div>My read on history is that movements explicit aiming for radical systemic change are pretty rare before the 19th century, and when they do exist are mostly religious and anticipating an apocalypse. <br /> <br /> With that as a starting point, I think a movement or conspiracy within the patrician houses would be aimed at either somehow raising their own house to be equal in status to that of the dynasts, or initially pushing for some relatively small reforms to the system to improve the position of patricians. A more radical movement might then arise from it if the situation in the Realm became substantially more chaotic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3174-carl-ollivier","name":"Carl.ollivier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}